WEBVTT

00:00:03.625 --> 00:00:04.834
- Yah-ha!
- (Mrs Brown) Ooh!

00:00:05.417 --> 00:00:06.917
<i>Voilà!</i>

00:00:07.959 --> 00:00:10.375
Captain Hunter Cabot
at your service.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.584
Oh, Paddington Brown.
Pleased to meet you.

00:00:12.709 --> 00:00:14.709
Gina, tour.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:17.584
Tour? We have many tours available.

00:00:17.709 --> 00:00:21.000
We could see the pink dolphins?

00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:23.875
- Take in some Inca ruins?
- Feed the piranhas.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.875
(Both) Although it may cost you
an arm and a leg!

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.334
We need to go
to somewhere called Rumi Rock.

00:00:31.459 --> 00:00:33.459
Er... Rumi Rock?

00:00:33.584 --> 00:00:35.042
We don't go to Rumi Rock.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.125
Well, we could do with a tour...

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.250
We don't need this one.

00:00:40.042 --> 00:00:41.209
Yeah...

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:46.500
Well... I'm sorry, little bear,

00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:48.834
but you'll have to take your sightseeing
somewhere else.

00:00:48.959 --> 00:00:53.209
No, we're not sightseers.
It's an emergency, sir.

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:55.834
My Aunt Lucy has gone missing.

00:00:55.959 --> 00:00:58.667
Now she's out there somewhere,
all alone.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:04.375
I'm her only family...
and I've lost her.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:09.000
Please can you make an exception,
just this once?

00:01:15.959 --> 00:01:19.167
(Judy) University application travelogue.

00:01:19.292 --> 00:01:23.209
Day two. We head off the tourist trail
and into the jungle,

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:26.125
our fates in the hands
of the charming Captain Cabot

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.667
and his daughter Gina.

00:01:27.792 --> 00:01:30.209
(Blows horn)

00:01:31.292 --> 00:01:35.167
Hey, Judy, take a photo with all this,
for the dudes back at the office.

00:01:35.292 --> 00:01:36.125
Dudes?

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.000
Just take the photo.

00:01:41.459 --> 00:01:43.667
Well, your cabins are ready.

00:01:43.792 --> 00:01:46.625
From now on,
you must follow my orders.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:50.167
To the inexperienced,
a boat can pose many dangers...

00:01:50.292 --> 00:01:51.125
Boom!

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:53.959
Thank you, Gina!

00:01:54.084 --> 00:01:56.000
She has to warn me.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.667
Every time!

00:01:59.792 --> 00:02:03.834
(♪ Plays "The Entertainer")

00:02:03.959 --> 00:02:06.500
(♪ Harmonising melody)

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:11.917
(Mr Brown) Funny man.

00:02:12.042 --> 00:02:13.709
Welcome aboard.

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:15.709
Who are these people?

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:19.584
Er... those are my ancestors,
the Cabots.

00:02:19.709 --> 00:02:22.542
(Mrs Brown) Gosh, that's quite
a family resemblance.

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:27.042
(Cabot) All the generations
from every corner of the globe.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:32.584
They like to keep an eye on me
just to make sure I bring glory on the family.

00:02:32.709 --> 00:02:34.417
That's like your tattoo.

00:02:34.542 --> 00:02:36.875
Oh, good spot, Mary.

00:02:37.542 --> 00:02:39.667
- What tattoo?
- Oh, he's got a tattoo...

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.709
It's the Cabot family crest,

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:43.792
the fist of gold.

00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:46.084
Very observant of you.

00:02:46.209 --> 00:02:47.750
A drunken night in Cusco, was it?

00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:49.709
- No.
- Ooh!

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:54.000
Well, this is a badge of pride.

00:02:54.125 --> 00:02:56.625
All the Cabots have this tattoo.

00:02:58.459 --> 00:03:01.292
This was a drunken night in Cusco.

00:03:01.417 --> 00:03:03.084
- (All gasp)
- (Cabot laughs)

00:03:05.209 --> 00:03:06.917
Follow me.

00:03:07.459 --> 00:03:10.625
And finally, the Darwin Suite.

00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:13.084
Oh, yes, well...

00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:16.209
- That's more like it.
- (Mrs Brown) Isn't it so charming?

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:22.334
The old purple kneed tarantula.

00:03:22.459 --> 00:03:26.792
It's... my husband's got
a bit of a thing about spiders and bugs.

00:03:26.917 --> 00:03:28.250
In fact, he's got a whole folder...

00:03:28.375 --> 00:03:30.459
Don't bother the Captain
with all that, darling.

00:03:30.584 --> 00:03:31.584
No, sorry.

00:03:34.542 --> 00:03:36.959
- Enjoy.
- Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:03:37.084 --> 00:03:38.584
It's so nice.

00:03:39.542 --> 00:03:44.042
- Looks like a nice firm mattress.
- Yes. Lovely.

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:07.167
Rumi Rock, huh?

00:04:07.292 --> 00:04:09.417
Do not fail us this time.

00:04:09.542 --> 00:04:11.875
<i>Uno, dos, tres, cuatro, cinco,
seis, siete, ocho, nueve, diez.</i>

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.750
<i>Uno, dos, tres, cuatro, cinco,
seis, siete, ocho, nueve...</i>

00:04:17.917 --> 00:04:21.500
I was going through my bag,
and look what I found: Travel Scrabble.

00:04:21.625 --> 00:04:24.334
It's your favourite, isn't it?
Quick game?

00:04:24.459 --> 00:04:27.084
Mum, I really need to work
on my travelogue.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:28.917
Oh.

00:04:32.959 --> 00:04:34.709
"Travelogue"...

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:38.125
Fourteen points.
That's without the triple word score.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.834
(Chuckling)

00:04:45.875 --> 00:04:48.125
(Paddington) 'I can't keep the line, Mrs Bird.'

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.209
You're breaking up, dear.

00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:54.959
Mr Brown says these satellite phone calls
are very expensive.

00:04:55.084 --> 00:04:56.750
- What?
- 'Expensive!'

00:04:56.875 --> 00:04:59.292
E-X-P...

00:04:59.417 --> 00:05:01.292
Ugh! It's gone again!

00:05:02.125 --> 00:05:05.584
Oh, these satellite phones
are very temperamental.

00:05:05.709 --> 00:05:08.792
Oh, no! No...
No, no, it's not that. It's...

00:05:09.417 --> 00:05:14.209
It's like this building is filled
with electrical interference.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.542
It's a very old building, Mrs Bird.

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:18.500
Nothing suspicious about it.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:21.792
Suspicious?

00:05:27.542 --> 00:05:30.292
Oh. Oh, knees...

00:05:30.417 --> 00:05:33.000
What are you telling me?

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.292
Has there been any news
of Aunt Lucy?

00:05:37.417 --> 00:05:39.709
Oh... no, dear, I'm afraid not.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.042
(Sighs)

00:05:43.959 --> 00:05:46.125
We'll find her, Paddington.

